{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NLX4xNWZSKsz6FLDL3VgNK","type":"tool_result","content":"total 16\ndrwx------@     4 brenn  staff      128 Nov 21 13:20 .\ndrwx------@ 33217 brenn  staff  1062944 Nov 21 13:20 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@    14 brenn  staff      448 Oct  2 03:50 agent\n-rw-r--r--@     1 brenn  staff     5368 Nov 21 13:20 sheet.md\n# Independent coverage discovery: A01 — Distinct agent identity\n\nEstablish your own findings from the code before comparing with any earlier\nreview. You are not told the earlier rating, answers, citations or exceptions.\n**Requirement:** Give the agent its own verifiable non-human identity, separate from the user who launched it and from unrelated agents. Preserve any explicitly delegated user/system subject separately and bound the authority used. Show that operators can revoke the agent's access independently of that subject, even when a user starts the run.\n**N/A condition:** never\n\nInventory all relevant paths/fields, including indirect paths, helpers and both directions of\nhandoffs. For each check, record coverage rows (subject, status enforced/missing/\nunclear/not_applicable, evidence, exact quote, note), deviations (required-control\nomissions; empty only if none), and concrete falsification attempts (category,\ninput, trace, outcome blocked/accepted/unclear/not_applicable, evidence, quote).\nSmall or residual omissions are still omissions. A missing row or unresolved\ncoverage cannot support holds. Do not run repository code; derive counterexamples\nby tracing it. A bounded_after budget claim needs a finite overshoot bound, not\njust a shared counter. Exemptions need quoted scope evidence.\n\nSet applicability absent/present/unclear, with top-level evidence, quote and a\nsearch explanation. Absent must satisfy the exact N/A condition. When present,\nverdict is failed if any required check fails, unclear if any is unresolved,\notherwise upheld. Copy broken words from the requirement into violates.\n\n\n## A01.1\n\n**Check:** The agent runs under its own workload principal (service account, IAM role, SPIFFE ID, or agent ID) that no other service or unrelated agent uses.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find the agent's identity: pod `serviceAccountName`, IAM role, SPIFFE ID, or agent ID in IaC or deploy config. 2) Search other deployments, services, and agents in the repo for the same name or role. 3) Answer no if it is shared, `default`, the main backend's identity, or only a string label with no credential. Answer unknown if identity is assigned outside this repo.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## A01.2\n\n**Check:** Tool and API clients use short-lived credentials with a verified acting-agent identity and any separately bounded user/system delegation; they do not copy a login session or reuse a gateway token at a different backend audience.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Trace every client credential to its issuer, audience, acting principal and delegated subject. 2) Accept authorized OAuth delegation and supported exchange when agent identity and bounded grants survive. 3) Reject copied sessions, shared static keys, or cross-audience token reuse. 4) Mark issuer/downstream guarantees unknown if only external evidence can show them.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## A01.3\n\n**Check:** For user-initiated runs, the original user is a verified delegated subject while the acting agent retains its own principal.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Trace user-started runs and credential issuance, including OAuth delegation and token exchange where supported. 2) Check original subject, acting agent and granted task/tenant/resource limits independently. 3) Reject a user label from model-controlled input or replacement of agent identity with a human session. 4) For machine-only operation, cite the configuration showing there is no delegated user; do not invent one.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## A01.4\n\n**Check:** Permissions are bound to the agent principal in IaC or RBAC, so revoking that principal alone removes the agent's access without disabling the user.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find IAM policies, RoleBindings, or grants in Terraform, Helm, or Kubernetes YAML. 2) Check they bind to the agent principal, not to a user, group, or shared role. 3) Check that removing that binding alone would cut the agent's access. 4) Answer no if revoking the agent cannot remove its access independently, or authority uses a shared credential. User grants may legitimately bound an explicitly delegated flow. Answer unknown if permissions are not defined in this repo.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to A01.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"A01\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"A01.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\", \"coverage\": [], \"deviations\": [], \"attempts\": []}],\n \"applicability\": \"absent | present | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\",\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\nagent\nagent/migrations\nagent/migrations/001_init.sql\nagent/requirements.txt\nagent/config\nagent/config/agent.yaml\nagent/config/tools.yaml\nagent/Dockerfile\nagent/k8s\nagent/k8s/deployment.yaml\nagent/k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml\nagent/k8s/admission.yaml\nagent/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\nagent/CODEOWNERS\nagent/.mcp.json\nagent/release\nagent/release/manifest.yaml\nagent/README.md\nagent/.github\nagent/.github/workflows\nagent/.github/workflows/release.yml\nagent/prompts\nagent/prompts/system.md\nagent/src\nagent/src/killswitch.py\nagent/src/gateway_client.py\nagent/src/gateway.py\nagent/src/audit.py\nagent/src/approvals.py\nagent/src/credentials.py\nagent/src/tools.py\nagent/src/type_id.py\nagent/src/redact.py\nagent/src/retrieval.py\nagent/src/agent.py\nagent/src/budgets.py\nagent/src/main.py\nagent/src/validation.py","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a3319f45-445c-413d-9771-d5bdb944cf4e","uuid":"c83a6d74-bd93-4d66-8ee7-4606c5c7c096","timestamp":"2026-11-21T12:20:25.014Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"total 16\ndrwx------@     4 brenn  staff      128 Nov 21 13:20 .\ndrwx------@ 33217 brenn  staff  1062944 Nov 21 13:20 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@    14 brenn  staff      448 Oct  2 03:50 agent\n-rw-r--r--@     1 brenn  staff     5368 Nov 21 13:20 sheet.md\n# Independent coverage discovery: A01 — Distinct agent identity\n\nEstablish your own findings from the code before comparing with any earlier\nreview. You are not told the earlier rating, answers, citations or exceptions.\n**Requirement:** Give the agent its own verifiable non-human identity, separate from the user who launched it and from unrelated agents. Preserve any explicitly delegated user/system subject separately and bound the authority used. Show that operators can revoke the agent's access independently of that subject, even when a user starts the run.\n**N/A condition:** never\n\nInventory all relevant paths/fields, including indirect paths, helpers and both directions of\nhandoffs. For each check, record coverage rows (subject, status enforced/missing/\nunclear/not_applicable, evidence, exact quote, note), deviatio